{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310606,"nonce":"PW7MHDZObId6zGzvo9NVc5O2Y/M=","title":"2026-09-24 e7315c43 (623-\u003e624) — Issue4886 lost by 52585dd3's \\\"Array\u003cDynamic\u003e element is a box\\\" rule; the Dynamic was a DECAY from a ...","message":"**e7315c43, conformance 623 -\u003e 624, issue 68eae570.**\n\n- 52585dd3 made an `Array\u003cDynamic\u003e` element load as a box pointer. Issue4886 broke because its array was only Dynamic by DECAY: a FIELD INITIALIZER is typed during class registration, before the callee's body infers its return. Same order-dependence as [[bugs_forward_declared_return_type_decays]]; the fix lives in the same place (classes.rs pre-registration, `anonymous_return_type_from_ast` now follows `return v` to `var v = {...}` via the shared `local_init`).\n- Anon-typed index reads loaded as plain I64 (`trace(arr[0])` printed an address). Now load as `Ptr(Void)` like any anon local.\n- `trace(v)` for ANY anonymous object printed `null` at HEAD: traceAny formats BOXES only. Trace now boxes anon via `maybe_box_value` (the Std.string path). NOT `box_value_for_dynamic`: it boxes anon through `haxe_box_class_instance`, which reads a class id from the header anon objects don't have (prints `\u003cunknown type N\u003e`).\n- Same hazard as ever ([[bugs_function_values_and_untyped_params_decayed_dynamic]]): a rule keyed on a declared `Dynamic` hits decays. Fixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/AnonReturnedThroughLocal.hx.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_field_init_anon_return_and_anon_trace` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}